## Agent harness

This repo ships an AI-agent setup that works across tools. The contract every agent reads
is **[`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md)** — start there.

| Tool | Entry point |
| --- | --- |
{% if include_claude -%}
| Claude Code | `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (imports `AGENTS.md`) + `.claude/skills/` |
{% endif -%}
| Codex / Cursor / Gemini / Aider / Zed | `AGENTS.md` (native) |
{% if include_copilot -%}
| GitHub Copilot | `.github/copilot-instructions.md` |
{% endif %}

### The one rule that keeps it portable

Skills and CI never name your stack — they call **tasks**. The {{ task_runner }} file is the
only place real commands live:

```bash
{% if task_runner == "just" %}just verify   # lint + typecheck + test{% elif task_runner == "make" %}make verify   # lint + typecheck + test{% elif task_runner == "npm" %}npm run verify   # lint + typecheck + test{% else %}# define lint / typecheck / test / build commands{% endif %}
```

### Skills

Skills are reusable agent know-how. The source of truth is **`.agents/skills/`**; the
`.claude/` and `.github/` copies are generated. After editing a skill:

```bash
{% if task_runner == "just" %}just sync-adapters{% else %}node tools/sync-adapters.mjs{% endif %}
```

Catalog: [`.agents/skills/README.md`](.agents/skills/README.md).

### Workflows

- **`plan`** — a focused, single-PR change (grills you first).
{% if include_sdd -%}
- **SDD pipeline** (`spec → plan → tasks → implement`) — features with real decisions.
  See [`docs/sdd-workflow.md`](docs/sdd-workflow.md).
- **`execute-tasks`** — run generated tasks in parallel, one integration PR.
{% endif -%}
{% if include_pr_review_ai -%}
- **`pr-review`** — multi-dimension review of a pull request.
{% endif -%}
- **`create-skill`** — author a domain skill for your stack.

## Getting started

1. Wire the {{ task_runner }} file so `verify` actually runs your stack.
2. Point your agent at the repo (see the table above).
3. Pick a workflow and go.

This repo was generated from [forge](https://github.com/nuccig/forge); pull later harness
improvements by re-scaffolding into a scratch directory and merging what you want.

